  "query_preview": "/Saturday through Wednesday/...\nIssued 301 AM MDT WED SEP 30 2026\nSouthwest flow aloft will develop Saturday and Sunday as the \nupper ridge axis shifts west and a weak low pressure approaches \nthe west coast. Valley temperatures will peak in the mid to \nupper 80s by Sunday with this enhanced southerly flow. Models \nindicate the weak low will briefly interrupt the ridge and move \nthrough the forecast area Monday. While NBM/WPC keep the \nprobability of precipitation near zero, some ensemble members do\nindicate an increase in precipitation chances at 10-15% over \nthe higher terrain in southwest/central Idaho due to the \npresence of marginal mid-level moisture. Thereafter, the ridge \nwill rebuild and promote warm, dry, and fair conditions across \nsoutheast Oregon and southwest Idaho during mid-week.",
